# GardenPulse API — manual requests
#
# Open this file in VS Code with the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
# and click "Send Request" above any request. Start the API first: npm run dev
#
# The requests follow a typical session from top to bottom. Named requests save
# values (tokens, ids) that later requests reuse, so run them in order:
#   1. "Register a user" and "Log in as a user"   → {{token}} (role user)
#   2. "Log in as the admin" (after npm run seed:admin) → {{adminToken}}
#   3. "Create a sensor" → {{sensorId}}

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

# Must match ADMIN_EMAIL and ADMIN_PASSWORD in your .env
@adminEmail = admin@example.com
@adminPassword = change-me-admin-password

### ===================== Health and errors =====================

### Health check → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Unknown route → 404 NotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist

### Malformed JSON body → 400 InvalidJSON
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email":

### ===================== Sign up and log in =====================

### Register a user → 201 with a token (a second run → 409 EmailAlreadyRegistered)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Gardener",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "plain-secret-123"
}

### Register asking for the admin role → 201, role "user" with adminRequest "pending"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Grace Planter",
  "email": "grace@example.com",
  "password": "plain-secret-123",
  "requestAdmin": true
}

### Register with invalid data → 400 ValidationError listing every field
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### Log in as a user → 200 with a JWT, saved as {{token}}
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "plain-secret-123"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.$.data.token}}

### Log in with a wrong password → 401 InvalidCredentials
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Current user → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Current user without a token → 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### Log in as the admin (run npm run seed:admin first) → token saved as {{adminToken}}
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.token}}

### ===================== Admin requests (admin only) =====================

### A regular user tries to list admin requests → 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/admin-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pending admin requests → 200 (the first one is saved as {{pendingUserId}})
# @name adminRequests
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/admin-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

@pendingUserId = {{adminRequests.response.body.$.data.users[0].id}}

### Approve the first pending request → 200, the user becomes admin
### (a second decision on the same user → 409 Conflict)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{pendingUserId}}/admin-request
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "approve" }

### ===================== Sensors =====================

### Create a sensor (admin) → 201 with a Location header; id saved as {{sensorId}}
# @name createSensor
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Tomato bed moisture",
  "type": "soil_moisture",
  "location": "Bed 3",
  "threshold": 25,
  "thresholdDirection": "below"
}

@sensorId = {{createSensor.response.body.$.data.sensor.id}}

### Create another sensor (admin): temperature, anomalous above 35 °C
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Greenhouse temperature",
  "type": "temperature",
  "location": "Greenhouse",
  "threshold": 35
}

### A regular user tries to create a sensor → 403 Forbidden
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Not allowed",
  "type": "light",
  "location": "Bed 1",
  "threshold": 1000
}

### Create a sensor with invalid data → 400 listing every field
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "type": "wind", "threshold": "high" }

### List sensors (any logged-in user) → 200 with pagination metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filter sensors by type and status
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors?type=soil_moisture&active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid sensor query → 400 listing every wrong parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors?page=0&type=wind
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sensor detail → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sensor that does not exist → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors/000000000000000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ===================== Readings (any logged-in user) =====================

### Record a normal reading → 201, anomalous: false; id saved as {{readingId}}
# @name createReading
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}/readings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": 31.5, "timestamp": "2026-10-18T10:00:00Z" }

@readingId = {{createReading.response.body.$.data.reading.id}}

### Record an anomalous reading (below the threshold of 25) → 201, anomalous: true
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}/readings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": 12, "timestamp": "2026-10-18T11:00:00Z" }

### Record another anomalous reading → 201, anomalous: true
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}/readings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": 18, "timestamp": "2026-10-18T12:00:00Z" }

### Try to set the anomaly from the client → ignored, the server decides (false)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}/readings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": 40, "timestamp": "2026-10-18T13:00:00Z", "anomalous": true }

### Record a reading for a sensor that does not exist → 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/000000000000000000000000/readings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": 12, "timestamp": "2026-10-18T11:00:00Z" }

### Reading with invalid data → 400 (value not a number, bad date)
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}/readings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": "dry", "timestamp": "yesterday" }

### Reading detail → 200 with its sensor and unit
GET {{baseUrl}}/readings/{{readingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reading history → newest first, 10 per page, with pagination metadata and next/prev links
GET {{baseUrl}}/readings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pagination + filters + sorting combined: anomalous soil moisture readings,
### lowest value first, 1 per page (page 2 of 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/readings?type=soil_moisture&anomalous=true&sort=value&page=2&limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Readings of one sensor in a date range, oldest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/readings?sensor={{sensorId}}&from=2026-10-18T00:00:00Z&to=2026-10-18T23:59:59Z&sort=timestamp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid history query → 400 listing every wrong parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/readings?anomalous=maybe&sort=name&limit=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ===================== Sensor updates and deletion (admin) =====================

### Update the threshold → 200; the anomaly flag of existing readings is recalculated
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "threshold": 15 }

### A regular user tries to update a sensor → 403 Forbidden
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hacked" }

### Change the type of a sensor with readings → 409 Conflict
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "temperature" }

### Delete a sensor with readings → 409 Conflict (nothing is deleted)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### A regular user tries to delete a sensor → 403 Forbidden
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete the sensor and all its readings → 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
